{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/57405-question-regarding-the-revenant-numina","id":57405,"title":"Question regarding the Revenant Numina","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-25T07:19:12-08:00","id":57405,"title":"Question regarding the Revenant Numina","content":"I'm attempting to reconcile the GMC rules for ghosts with the numina found in the Mummy ST Handbook. I'm having a hard time working out how Revenant is intended to work. It appears in the first paragraph of the numen description that the revenant's corpse becomes a mobile anchor. <br /> <br /> &quot;Its body is a mobile anchor allowing it to travel through the living world.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, the third paragraph suggests that the Untethered and Impassioned Soul numina hold some value, as they provide mobility. Are these two numina necessary for a revenant, or does it function as if it were always in proximity to its anchor, no matter where it goes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T08:23:45-08:00","id":57450,"title":"","content":"The revenant Numen is a sort of rules hack to turn ghosts into Revenants from World of Darkness: Antagonists.<br /> <br /> Under the GMC rules it does NOT turn your corpse into an anchor, but is a type of Claiming of a corpse. The main difference from Claim is that the resulting Revenant uses the Skills and Attributes of the host body and that the Revenant can keep using Numina. The Revenant probably loses access to its Manifestations and has to get the different Numen from Mummy instead.<br /> <br /> Untethered and Impassioned Soul are both listed because they are both part of the Revenant template from Antagonists. Untethered enables you to leave the vicinity of your Anchor, which can be quite handy because your body is not necessarily your anchor (being your own corpse). I would rules that to posess another corpse than your own, it has to be a permanent Anchor to the ghost, limiting the ghost to the Intruder Numen if he wants to steal random bodies.<br /> <br /> Impassioned Soul gives freedom from Morality, Virtue and Vice in exchange for becoming ruled by his Passions. This also gives him a new avenue to restore his Essence.<br /> <br /> The main reason of existence for a Revenant is to take revenge or otherwise resolve his unfinished business, which is why most Revenants have Impassioned Soul. The Revenant already has a set of objectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":".  spelling 01-25-2014, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T08:33:23-08:00","id":57454,"title":"","content":"I understand the distinction between GMC and MtC rules. The question I have is more whether being a Revenant is sufficient in and of itself to be free of the need for other anchors, or if other support is required. Thank you for your help. This gives me some ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T12:01:19-08:00","id":58971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/57405-question-regarding-the-revenant-numina?p=57454#post57454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand the distinction between GMC and MtC rules. The question I have is more whether being a Revenant is sufficient in and of itself to be free of the need for other anchors, or if other support is required. Thank you for your help. This gives me some ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading Revenant, the Revenant can't leave the corpse. So Untethered does nothing for it at all, except perhaps provide a justification as to how it found and inhabited this corpse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T13:47:43-08:00","id":59094,"title":"","content":"Ghosts with Untethered and Impassioned Soul have greater mobility than ghosts without, inhabitable body or no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:16:51-08:00","id":59126,"title":"","content":"To elaborate on what Satchel said, the problem here is that the Revenant Numen in itself has no effect on the anchors of the ghost and the inability of the ghost to leave his anchors for an extended time. The body does not automatically become his anchor, and having a body as an anchor isn't exactly common. So to avoid having to cary his anchor everywhere and being vulnerable in case of the destuction of its anchor, the ghost can choose to take the Untethered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T16:09:02-08:00","id":59240,"title":"","content":"The numen description specifically states that the body becomes a mobile anchor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T17:09:44-08:00","id":59288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/57405-question-regarding-the-revenant-numina?p=59240#post59240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The numen description specifically states that the body becomes a mobile anchor.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do remember what happens to ghosts whose last anchor is destroyed, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T17:35:59-08:00","id":59311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/57405-question-regarding-the-revenant-numina?p=59288#post59288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do remember what happens to ghosts whose last anchor is destroyed, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Numina also explicitly states that the transformation is irreversible. The body must <i>already be</i> an anchor for the ghost, the ghost can't leave, and if the body is destroyed the ghost is kaput.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T18:10:43-08:00","id":59345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egarwaen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/57405-question-regarding-the-revenant-numina?p=59311#post59311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Numina also explicitly states that the transformation is irreversible. The body must <i>already be</i> an anchor for the ghost, the ghost can't leave, and if the body is destroyed the ghost is kaput.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the prerequisites for Impassioned Soul consist entirely of Untethered. Impassioned Soul is also known as &quot;that Numen that replicates revenants having Passions that they get Essence for following.&quot;<br /> <br /> The extra ghost rules in Mummy are unfortunately kludgey. This is known.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T11:58:01-08:00","id":60012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/57405-question-regarding-the-revenant-numina?p=59345#post59345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the prerequisites for Impassioned Soul consist entirely of Untethered. Impassioned Soul is also known as &quot;that Numen that replicates revenants having Passions that they get Essence for following.&quot;<br /> <br /> The extra ghost rules in Mummy are unfortunately kludgey. This is known.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree; and I think that's why Untethered and Impassioned Soul are called out - so that a Revenant can have Impassioned Soul, or at least Untethered to explain how it found this new body, without paying points it will never need again.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the text around the &quot;free Untethered&quot; bit makes it sound like there's more going on, which is good and strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}